f905ab8","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_pointwise_convergence_3a88e4ad_011","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"For $n\\ge1$, define $f_n(x)=n/(nx+1)$ on the common domain $(0,\\infty)$. Which calculation correctly finds the pointwise limit at the fixed point $x=2$?","options":["$\\dfrac{n}{2n+1}\\to1$, because numerator and denominator both tend to infinity.","$\\dfrac{n}{2n+1}=\\dfrac{1}{2+1/n}\\to\\dfrac{1}{2}$.","$\\dfrac{n}{2n+1}=\\dfrac{1}{1+1/(2n)}\\to1$.","$\\dfrac{n}{2n+1}=\\dfrac{1}{2}$ for every $n$, because the constant $1$ is negligible."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"06fdec7b89dde1e88f9ff4f7","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_pointwise_convergence_39b6dcef_013","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For pointwise convergence, what must happen at each fixed $x\\in X$?","options":["The convergence rate is the same for every $x$.","Every $f_n$ is continuous.","The domains $X_n$ must be finite.","For every fixed $x\\in X$, $\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}f_n(x)=f(x)$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a9fcf33fbc3965f3b50ff194","time_limit":25,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_2a_math_iii_analysis_pointwise_convergence_39b6dcef_014","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"In pointwise convergence, what is held fixed when taking the limit?","options":["The index $n$.","The whole graph shape.","The point $x$.","The derivative of $f_n$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3706f9e700d29efffb3095a3","time_limit":20,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00"